version³13³1ts³11105304235³1cache_oldmajor³17³1cache_oldauthor³17³1revision³18³1cache_diff_default_author³11³1tscreate³11074755832³1text_default³1version³21³2ts³21105304235³2ip³2217.247.140.107³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3+ links³3text³3= Society and Community =

A seemingly robust strategy of development is forming ancap communities or societies where the advantages of cooperation can be leveraged, but such is still in its infancy.

While the advantages of free society and the destructive or weakening effect of government on society have been noted and even generally acknowledged, the development of ancap society remains problematic. This seems due primarily to two difficulties. One, there is a large individualist component in the development of ancap. And two, the use of and trust in 'societal' actions or solutions has atrophied due to the vast array of state-generated and state-imposed structures.

However, one item on the horizon is the [http://freestateproject.org/index.jsp Free State Project], a major attempt at developing a collocated group of freedom-seeking individuals. The effects and continuing development are eagerly watched, even if freedom-seeking is not absolutely congruent with ancap-seeking.

That, even with its reputation, does not belittle other activities some of which have been on-going for years.

Here you will find not only an attempt at reportage and listing of some these actions, but also the hope of engendering both support for those existing and more attempts to form such society.

&nbsp;

